# Databases — local dev data, not source
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lab data — audio, transcripts and run output
#
# autosave.sh runs `git add -A` after every edit, so an unignored
# lecture recording would be committed automatically and permanently.
# A 40-minute WAV is 200-400 MB; GitHub's per-file hard limit is 100 MB.
#
# Beyond size: classroom audio contains identifiable students, and we
# have no consent position and have not read Sarvam's terms on secondary
# use. Audio does not enter a shared repository until both are settled.
#
# Every directory's README.md stays tracked so the structure and the
# regeneration command survive.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Projects/*/lab/data/**
!Projects/*/lab/data/**/
!Projects/*/lab/data/**/README.md
!Projects/*/lab/data/README.md

# Media, wherever it lands
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.aac
*.wma
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi
*.webm

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor and OS junk
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Temporary
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
.knowledge-bootstrap/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BuilderOS runtime — never commit these.
# End-Session's Inbox lock is a transient per-run file (pid + start time).
# It must never enter a commit: Phase 8 stages AI-Memory/Inbox/, and a
# committed lock would look "held" to the next run on a fresh clone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AI-Memory/Inbox/.lock

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Product evaluation output and design-loop runs
#
# Added 2026-09-09, after autosave committed 252 files including 109
# screenshots of the running app and six evaluation JSONs — locally only,
# and caught before the push, but armed the whole time.
#
# The mechanism was already understood: the block above says autosave runs
# `git add -A` after every edit, and each product tree's own .gitignore
# repeats it above `fixtures/evaluation/`. These two paths were simply never
# added to either list, and the 2026-09-07 session avoided the problem by
# staging selectively — which left the hole open rather than closing it.
#
# What they hold: `.eval/` is model answers over real course and lecture
# content; `design-loop/runs/` is PNG screenshots of the app with that
# content rendered on screen, 144 MB of it. Both are lecture-derived, and
# this repository is public. Publishing either is a deliberate act with a
# consent question attached, not a side effect of saving a file.
#
# READMEs stay tracked so the structure and the regeneration command survive,
# exactly as for lab data above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.eval/
**/design-loop/runs/
!**/design-loop/runs/README.md

# Word/Office lock files
~$*

# Disposable security-audit copy of v4 — a strict duplicate of product/classmind-v4.
# progress.md (2026-09-09) records it as disposable; two copies of security-critical
# source is how "which one is real?" becomes a live question for a reader of this repo.
Projects/classmind/product/classmind-v4 - sECURE aUDIT/
